{"_provenance":"smoke17 (v2026.12.0 node smoke, 2026-11-04) smoke17 probe-paused.jsonl line 21, label B4.conq: query(domain='conquest_targets', character_id=13191); the reply's result as the 2026.12.0 server compacted it (38,481 characters as tool-result text)","args":{"domain":"conquest_targets","character_id":13191},"chars":38481,"result":{"action":"query_conquest_targets","ruler_id":13191,"duchy_count":94,"expansion_count":93,"toward_count":0,"conquerable_count":29,"target_count":388,"include_expansion":true,"engine_checks_done":3,"engine_checks_truncated":true,"note":"Conquest targets by de-jure duchy. Pass toward=<title key> (county to empire) to list every de-jure duchy under that title, anywhere on the map (in_toward=true, listed first); without it the duchies are the ones you partly hold (partially_held=true) and the ones bordering your realm (expansion_target=true). Each remaining county names its holder and his INDEPENDENT top liege (holder_top_liege_id: the one to war), the relation gates (independent, kin, allied, truced, already at war) and conquerable_now. conquerable_now comes from the engine's own county_conquest_cb check (conquerable_now_source=engine_county_conquest_cb), which carries the game's neighbour and sea-reach rules; engine_valid_cbs lists every other CB the engine accepts against that holder (invasion, claim, holy war, de jure...), so a county too far for a conquest war can still show the war that reaches it: weigh them with cbs(target_id). Without an engine check the verdict is the relation gates plus the county neighbour graph (conquerable_now_source=heuristic) and block_reason=not_adjacent_unverified marks the counties the check did not reach: raise max_engine_checks (<=16, default 3, ~0.8 s each) for more. A conquerable county carries a declare block for declare_war (county_conquest_cb, cb_title_id = the county) and a duchy_conquest_cb option for the whole duchy. The engine checks run on the game thread in either clock state.","duchie